      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both ground pins on each isolated CAN transceiver are connected to the same GND net: U10.4 (GND1) and U10.5 (GND2), and U11.4 (GND1) and U11.5 (GND2).",
      "expected": "The primary-side and CAN-side grounds should remain separate to preserve galvanic isolation, as intended for the isolated CAN interfaces.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "GND [...] U10.4(GND1,power_in) U10.5(GND2,power_in) U11.4(GND1,power_in) U11.5(GND2,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "each driven through an isolated CAN transceiver"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Tying the transceivers' two ground domains together defeats galvanic isolation, allowing ground-potential differences and common-mode disturbances on the CAN side to couple into the board.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The CAN transceivers’ primary and bus-side ground pins are all tied to the same GND net. This contradicts the specified isolated CAN interfaces and defeats their galvanic isolation."
}

